SpendSigil::postCheck
├── given the config was never initialized
│   └── it should revert with PolicyNotInitialized
├── given the meter is max(global calldata-sum, balance-delta) over the executed call set
│   ├── when the calldata-sum exceeds the balance delta (a charged approve that moved no balance)
│   │   └── it should charge the calldata-sum
│   └── when the balance delta exceeds the calldata-sum (an outflow the calldata parse missed)
│       └── it should charge the balance delta
├── given a rolling period
│   ├── when two charges fall in the same window
│   │   └── it should accrue them cumulatively
│   └── when a charge falls after the window boundary
│       └── it should reset spent to zero before accruing
├── given the metered outflow would push cumulative spend over the cap
│   └── it should revert with SpendCapExceeded
├── given an approval the execution granted is left non-zero at post-check
│   └── it should revert with DanglingAllowance
├── given a blanket-grant call on the budgeted token (the ERC-20 allowance scan can't see it)
│   ├── when it is a permit (EIP-2612)
│   │   └── it should revert with BlanketGrantBlocked
│   ├── when it is a setApprovalForAll (ERC-721/1155 operator)
│   │   └── it should revert with BlanketGrantBlocked
│   ├── when it is an authorizeOperator (ERC-777)
│   │   └── it should revert with BlanketGrantBlocked
│   └── when it is a Permit2 approve of the budgeted token
│       └── it should revert with Permit2GrantBlocked
└── given an increaseAllowance on the budgeted token
    ├── when it is left un-reset at close
    │   └── it should revert with DanglingAllowance
    └── when it is reset to zero within the same batch
        └── it should charge the added value via the global calldata-sum
